        "title": "Operations Research - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Operations research (OR) is the discipline of making **optimal decisions** about real systems by reducing them to mathematics. The pipeline is always the same: take a messy decision (route trucks, staff a call center, schedule jobs, allocate capital), write it as a **model** (variables, objective, constraints), **solve** the model with an algorithm whose properties you understand, and then **interpret** the solution — including how it shifts when the world changes."
